# Ooda CLI — Command Reference

File: ooda/docs/COMMANDS.oot

The `ooda` binary has 13 in-process subcommands (in 4 subdirs: build, fix, fmt, token) and 3 external packages spawned as subprocesses (opm, lsp, mcp). List derived from `ooda/main.oo`. See `docs/argv.oot` for flag grammar and `docs/dispatch.oot` for the lifecycle.

## In-process: build cluster

### ooda build

Compile a `.oo` file with `oodac`.

```sh
ooda build src/main.oo --target llvm -O2 -o build/main
ooda build src/main.oo --release --lto
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `ooda/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_build`. Positional: the `.oo` file. Flags: `--target`, `-o`, `-O0..-O3`, `-Oz`, `-Opgo`, `--lto`, `--release`, `--pgo-generate`, `--pgo-use=`, `-fsanitize=`, `--fuzz`. Unknown flags fail closed. Exit: 0 ok; 2 missing/bad; 1 subprocess failure.

### ooda run

Compile and run a `.oo` file.

```sh
ooda run src/main.oo
ooda run src/main.oo --engine=bc
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `ooda/build/host_build.oo::run_oodac_run`. Flag: `--engine {native,bc,...}`. Exit: 0 ok; 2 residual `--json-errors`; 1 run failure.

### ooda gen

Scaffold a new `.oo` file (module, service, or test) with an Academy header.

```sh
ooda gen module User
ooda gen service TokenLedger
ooda gen test User
```

Caps: FsWrite. Source: `ooda/build/gen.oo::run_ooda_gen`. Positional: subcommand + entity name. Exit: 0 ok; rejects names with `/` or `..`.

### ooda test

Compile and run a single `.oo` test file. Emits real JSON on `--json`.

```sh
ooda test tests/test_main.oo
ooda test tests/test_main.oo --engine=bc --json
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env, Time. Source: `ooda/build/test.oo::run_ooda_test`. Flags: `--engine=bc` / `-bc`, `--json` / `-json`. Exit: 0 pass; 1 fail; 2 missing/unknown.

### ooda install

Install a pre-built openOODA release pack into an XDG prefix. Requires `OODA_FS_WRITEDIR`.

```sh
ooda install --from ./build/pack --to $HOME
ooda install            # uses OODA_CHECKOUT, OODA_FS_WRITEDIR
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `ooda/build/install.oo::run_ooda_install_cmd`. Flags: `--from <path>`, `--to <path>`. Exit: 0 ok; 1 bad path or non-pack.

### ooda bench

Time `oodac check` (and optionally `oodac run`) on a `.oo` file.

```sh
ooda bench src/main.oo
ooda bench src/main.oo --run
```

Caps: FsRead, Process, Env, Time. Source: `ooda/build/bench.oo::run_ooda_bench`. Flag: `--run`. Exit: 0 ok; 2 missing; 1 check fail.

### ooda init

Bootstrap a new project layout (src/, tests/, ooda.pkg).

```sh
ooda init myapp
ooda init               # uses "myproject"
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite. Source: `ooda/build/init.oo::cli_init_project`. Positional: project name (default `myproject`). Exit: 0 ok; 1 bad name or existing path.

### ooda context

List `.oo` files under a path, or stream the AI codex to stdout.

```sh
ooda context .
ooda context src --json
ooda context --llm
```

Caps: FsRead. Source: `ooda/build/context.oo::run_ooda_context`. Positional: optional dir (default `.`). Flags: `--llm` (stream codex), `--json` (JSON listing). Exit: 0 ok.

### ooda health

Print the health line. Editors use it to verify ooda is on `$PATH`.

```sh
ooda health
```

Caps: FsRead, Env. Source: `ooda/build/health.oo::run_ooda_health`. Output: `ooda health: ok` and `OODA_COMPILER: yes|no`. Exit: 0.

## In-process: fix cluster

### ooda fix

Check a file, then apply at most 8 edits of kind E_CAP, E_TC, E_PARSE, E_IMP, or E_MUST. Write requires `--yes`.

```sh
ooda fix src/main.oo --dry-run
ooda fix src/main.oo --yes
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Env. Source: `ooda/fix/fix.oo::run_ooda_fix`. Flags: `--dry-run`, `--yes`. Exit: 0 ok; 1 no `--yes` or no supported diag; 2 bad path.

### ooda digest

Print the SHA-256 of a file.

```sh
ooda digest src/main.oo
```

Caps: FsRead. Source: `ooda/fix/digest.oo::run_ooda_digest`. Output: 64 hex chars. Exit: 0 ok; silent on missing/unreadable.

## In-process: fmt cluster

### ooda fmt

Format `.oo` files in place under strict idempotence and cap audit.

```sh
ooda fmt src/main.oo
ooda fmt --all
ooda fmt --check src/main.oo
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Alloc. Source: `ooda/fmt/fmt.oo::run_ooda_fmt`. Flags: `--check`, `--all`. Exit: 0 clean/rewrite; non-zero on bad file, missing cap, or non-idempotent.

## In-process: token cluster

### ooda token

Run a capability-token sub-subcommand. JSON is the default; `--human` switches to human-readable.

```sh
ooda token status
ooda token status --human
ooda token report
ooda token audit src/main.oo
ooda token query --baseline=v0.210
ooda token ask "what is the efficiency baseline?"
ooda token schema
ooda token diff before.oo after.oo
ooda token tail --lines=20
ooda token fix src/main.oo
ooda token snapshot
ooda token enforce
ooda token extra
```

Caps: FsRead, FsWrite, Process, Time. Source: `ooda/token/cmd_token.oo::run_ooda_token`. Positional: sub-subcommand name. Flags: `--human` / `-h`, `--format=human`, `--format=json`. Exit: 0 ok; sub-subcommand-defined.

The 12 sub-subcommands: `status`, `report`, `audit`, `query`, `ask`, `schema`, `diff`, `tail`, `fix`, `snapshot`, `enforce`, `extra`. Each has its own `cmd_*.oo` file under `ooda/token/`.

## Spawned: external packages

These spawn a subprocess and inherit stdio. The ooda binary does not link these packages.

### ooda opm

Delegate to the `opm` package manager.

```sh
ooda opm add foo
ooda opm audit
ooda opm launch --exec foo
```

Source: spawn `opm` at `$OODACODEX/bin/opm` only. Exit: whatever `opm` exits with. OODACODEX is required.

### ooda lsp

Delegate to the `lsp` LSP server.

```sh
ooda lsp                     # stdio mode (the editor case)
ooda lsp request.txt         # one-shot file mode
```

Source: spawn `lsp` at `$OODACODEX/bin/lsp` only. Exit: whatever `lsp` exits with. OODACODEX is required.

### ooda mcp

Delegate to the `mcp` MCP server.

```sh
ooda mcp                     # stdio mode
ooda mcp --file request.txt  # one-shot file mode
```

Source: spawn `mcp` via `$OODACODEX/bin/mcp` (stdio inherited). Exit: whatever `mcp` exits with. OODACODEX is required.
